  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "",
    "constraints": [
      "You are given NNN distinct points on a two-dimensional plane. It is guaranteed that no three of them are collinear. Let's call a subset of these points compact if the convex hull of this subset has exactly four vertices.",
      "Find the number of compact non-empty subsets of the given points. Since this number may be very large, compute it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
      "1≤N≤3001 \\le N \\le 3001≤N≤300",
      "∣x∣,∣y∣≤109|x|, |y| \\le 10^9∣x∣,∣y∣≤109",
      "no two points coincide and no three points are collinear",
      "Example Input 1`4",
      "0 0",
      "100 0",
      "0 100",
      "100 100",
      "`Example Output 1`1",
      "`Example Input 2`5",
      "0 0",
      "100 0",
      "0 100",
      "100 100",
      "50 60",
      "`Example Output 2`4",
      "`"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nEach of the next NNN lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy denoting the coordinates of one point.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing one integer ― the number of compact subsets modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
